From: LoMo <lomo@aviumui.org>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:33:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BackAnimationController: Yield close transition to remote/default handlers when targets are empty

When predictive back preview does not have targets (mApps is null or empty,
e.g. for non-predictive-back apps like QQ or WeChat), do not consume the
transition immediately with applyAndFinish(). Instead, clean up internal state
and return false, allowing RemoteTransitionHandler (Launcher3) and
DefaultTransitionHandler to play natural app-to-home exit animations.
---
 .../com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java  | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java
index 14d4cd18..19e5bd36 100644
--- a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java
@@ -1396,9 +1396,12 @@ public class BackAnimationController implements RemoteCallable<BackAnimationCont
 
             if (mApps == null || mApps.length == 0) {
                 if (mCloseTransitionRequested) {
-                    // animation never start, consume directly
-                    applyAndFinish(st, ft, finishCallback);
-                    return true;
+                    // Predictive back preview never started or has no targets; let remote
+                    // or default transition handlers animate the app exit instead of
+                    // consuming the transition with zero animation.
+                    mCloseTransitionRequested = false;
+                    applyFinishOpenTransition();
+                    return false;
                 } else if (mClosePrepareTransition == null
                         && info.getType() == WindowManager.TRANSIT_PREPARE_BACK_NAVIGATION) {
                     // Gesture animation was cancelled before prepare transition ready, create
